---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
const repo = "https://github.com/tidus747/planacity";
const later = [
  [
    "v0.6",
    "Milestones & Deliveries",
    "Represent program outcomes, readiness dependencies, and delivery risk.",
  ],
  [
    "v0.7",
    "Communication",
    "Share timelines, capacity, calendars, and a Program Pack outside the application.",
  ],
  [
    "v0.8",
    "Scenarios & Reconciliation",
    "Compare alternatives and reconcile Jira re-imports without losing the baseline.",
  ],
  [
    "v0.9",
    "Stabilisation",
    "Focus on reliability, performance, keyboard access, migrations, and installers.",
  ],
  [
    "v1.0",
    "A dependable planning loop",
    "Import, structure, schedule, allocate, validate, communicate, and export.",
  ],
];
---

<Page
  title="Roadmap"
  description="The Planacity roadmap: reliable planning, explainable capacity, team visibility, and small, reviewable releases."
>
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE ROAD AHEAD</p>
      <h1>
        Small releases.
        <br />
        Useful progress.
      </h1>
      <p>
        A clear direction, shaped by real planning work. Each step should make
        one more part of the program easier to understand.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="doc-grid">
      <aside class="doc-nav" aria-label="Roadmap sections">
        <p>In this roadmap</p>
        <a href="#available">Available today</a>
        <a href="#current">v0.5 / Current focus</a>
        <a href="#next">v0.5 / File imports</a>
        <a href="#later">Beyond the preview</a>
        <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>Track GitHub issues</a>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="notice">
          <strong>Current target: v0.5 Program Calendar</strong>
          <p>
            This is a development preview, not a published stable release. The
            roadmap describes direction, not promised delivery dates.
          </p>
        </div>
        <section id="available">
          <h2>A working foundation</h2>
          <p>Available in the source preview:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Local project files, JSON backups, a hierarchical Plan editor, and
              filters.
            </li>
            <li>
              Jira CSV import/export, field mappings, and imported baseline
              comparison.
            </li>
            <li>
              Timeline scales, grouping, filters, dependency arrows, Team mode,
              a selected-work graph, critical-path analysis, and date editing.
            </li>
            <li>
              People, work calendars, dated availability, recurring duties,
              one-person executable-work assignments, and exact capacity views.
            </li>
            <li>
              Estimate units in hours, days, or weeks, with calendar setup in
              the same dialog.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            These foundations are implemented. Shared holidays and program
            events now participate in capacity calculations and have a dedicated
            editor; visual projection is the active work.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="current">
          <h2>Now: put program events in context.</h2>
          <p>
            Development proceeds through focused issues, one at a time. The
            source version remains 0.4.0.dev0 until a release change is
            reviewed.
          </p>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">v0.5 A</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Team visibility - complete</h3>
              <p>
                Team Timeline lanes, availability overlays, dependency cards,
                stable work identity, and critical-path analysis are available.
              </p>
              <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md`}>
                Review the detailed roadmap
              </a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">v0.5 B</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Program Calendar - in progress</h3>
              <p>
                The shared-event domain, schema 12 persistence, capacity
                effects, and Calendar editor are complete. Timeline/Overview
                projection comes next, without turning duties into fictitious
                appointments.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">v0.4</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Team &amp; Capacity - complete in source</h3>
              <p>
                Capacity findings, People breakdowns, Overview analysis, work
                context, priorities, and single-person assignments are
                available.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </section>
        <section id="next">
          <h2>Then: import availability safely.</h2>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">v0.5 C</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Generic availability CSV</h3>
              <p>
                Preview mappings, match people explicitly, identify duplicates,
                and retain ambiguous rows for correction instead of guessing.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">v0.5 D</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Factorial exported files</h3>
              <p>
                Adapt exported files to the same reviewed import workflow. Keep
                provider terminology outside the canonical planning model and
                avoid storing unnecessary HR detail.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </section>
        <section id="later">
          <h2>Beyond the preview</h2>
          {later.map(([version, title, description]) => (
            <article class="release">
              <span class="release-tag">{version}</span>
              <div>
                <h3>{title}</h3>
                <p>{description}</p>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </section>
        <div class="notice">
          <strong>Follow the decisions, not just the feature list.</strong>
          <p>
            The{" "}
            <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md`}>
              implementation roadmap
            </a>{" "}
            defines issue scope and acceptance.{" "}
            <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/planning-decisions.md`}>
              Planning decisions
            </a>{" "}
            explain calculation rules and data integrity. Live progress belongs
            in <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>GitHub Issues</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Page>
